# The perception service image (src/medomni/perception/sidecar/Dockerfile) is the one build with the repository root
# as its context. BuildKit reads that Dockerfile's own Dockerfile.dockerignore; Docker's legacy builder reads only this
# file, so the two carry the same rules (tests/perception/test_sidecar.py checks it). Encoder builds stage their own
# contexts, and task environments build from their atom folder, so neither reads this file.
# Only what the Dockerfile copies: the encoders' weights (*/assets), test data and runtime state stay out.
*
!pyproject.toml
!src/medomni/__init__.py
!src/medomni/core
!src/medomni/perception
!core/families
# the legacy builder can't re-include a file through a wildcard folder, so: the encoder tree, nothing inside an
# encoder folder, then its three files
!perception/encoders
perception/encoders/*/*/*
!perception/encoders/*/*/card.yaml
!perception/encoders/*/*/adapter.py
!perception/encoders/*/*/Dockerfile
!perception/deployed.yaml
!perception/deployment.yaml
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
